## The headline findings

**1. The token conversation is mostly not about memory.** From your real 40 days of transcripts (33 sessions, 3,360 requests, 656M tokens ≈ $868 API-equivalent): **~85% of cost is context movement** — cache reads 51-57%, cache writes 22-34%, actual output only 15-21%. Median request drags 153k tokens of resident context. Top 5 sessions = 69% of all spend. Order of levers: **context hygiene ≫ delegation ≫ model routing ≫ memory diet**.

**2. Distill's ledger, measured to the cent:** all-in overhead ≈ **5-6% of spend** (~$50/window: /distill turns $30, subagent ~$6-18, SPINE carry $12). Savings side: encoded *environment gotchas* show **~zero recurrence after encoding** (index.lock, NTFS colons, python3 stub, cp1252 — all one-and-done), but *behavioral rules* recur regardless (edit-before-read: 25× despite encoding) — your execution-gap thesis, now quantified. Friction savings alone ($10-30) don't repay the $50; the big claimed saving (avoided re-derivation) has **no counterfactual in the data**. Honest published verdict: *overhead proven, savings directional — distill is a token shaper, not yet a proven saver.* Top follow-up: add token telemetry to distill-benchmark arms.

**3. Routing (blind-judged, adversarially reviewed pre-run):** mechanical transforms and extraction survived **Haiku untouched** — the one wrong extraction answer came from *Opus*. Comprehension needs Sonnet; adversarial judgment stays frontier. Haiku applied 4/5 in-context gotchas. Hidden tax: cheap models emit 3-7× more output tokens. And the E2 twist: an orchestrator already routes near-optimally *without* a routing file — **your monoculture is a habit gap, not a knowledge gap**, so the fix is structural (subagent `model:` defaults) not prose. Also: distill-learned routing has essentially **zero prior art** — genuinely novel territory if you want it.

## Per your decision frame

- **Free wins (no output change):** benchmark token telemetry, the transcript-mining methodology fix, `model:` frontmatter on read-only subagents.
- **Trade-off knobs (need your call + explicit opt-in):** diet SPINE (1.2k vs 3.6k: −29% read volume but held-out recall dropped 10/12 — a v2 "preserve distinctive nouns" rule is the next test); [ROUTE] markers in knowledge; context-cap discipline.

